}

' ===========================================================
' MODULE: community_worker (agent)
' ===========================================================
package "community_worker/agent" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {

  package "(existing)" <<Rectangle>> #fef3c7 {
    class "agent.py" as Agent {
      poll loop, every 5s
      GET /jobs/next-for-machine/{id}
    }
  }
}

' ===========================================================
' DESKTOP UI (Tauri renderer) — caller of the new endpoint
' ===========================================================
package "desktop frontend" <<Frame>> #f5e8ff {

  package "(new caller)" <<Rectangle>> #bbf7d0 {
    class "Available Machines page" as DesktopUI {
      GET /machines/available
      --
      Replaces the legacy /machines call.
      Sees exactly what the allocator
      would see on the next dispatch tick.
    }
  }
}

' ===========================================================
' MODULE: serverV2/infrastructure
' ===========================================================
package "serverV2/infrastructure" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {

  package "(existing)" <<Rectangle>> #fef3c7 {
    class RedisClient
    class "Postgres\nmachines table" as PgMachines {
      id, status, machine_type,
      gpu_vram_gb, last_seen_at, ...
    }
  }
}

' ===========================================================
' Per-poll write/read sequence (the self-heal flow)
' ===========================================================
Agent --> JobsRouter : GET /jobs/next-for-machine/{id} (every 5s)
JobsRouter --> JobService : next_for_machine(machine_id)

JobService --> Mirror : record(machine_id)
Mirror ..> RedisClient : ZADD machines:alive

JobService --> MachineService : ensure_available(machine_id)
MachineService --> Mirror : get_status(machine_id)
Mirror ..> RedisClient : HGET machines:status {id}

MachineService ..> MachineRepo : update_status(id, 'available')\n[only when status != 'available']
MachineRepo --> PgMachines : UPDATE machines SET status='available'
MachineRepo ..> Mirror : set_status(id, 'available')   <<async via executor>>
Mirror ..> RedisClient : HSET machines:status {id} 'available'

JobService --> JobsRouter : (continues to claim_next_for_machine)

' ===========================================================
' Available-machines read sequence (NEW — UI -> allocator's view)
' ===========================================================
DesktopUI --> MachinesRouter : GET /machines/available
MachinesRouter --> AllocationClient : list_available_machines()
AllocationClient --> AllocationFacade : list_available_machines()
AllocationFacade --> FleetAvailabilitySnapshotCache : get_or_build()
FleetAvailabilitySnapshotCache ..> Mirror : (allocator path uses\nMachineRedisMirror inside\nCommunityAvailabilityBuilder)

note right of FleetAvailabilitySnapshotCache
  This is the single source of truth.
  The allocator's strategies and the
  /machines/available endpoint both read
  THIS object — by definition they cannot
  disagree on which PCs are available
  for the next dispatch.
end note

' ===========================================================
' Other write surfaces — same pattern (PG sync, mirror async)
' ===========================================================
note as N1
  Every other status-write call site
  (set_processing, demote_ghosts,
  community-monitor flips) goes through
  MachineRepository now.  No call site
  ever talks to Mirror.set_status/clear_status
  directly except via the repo.
end note
N1 .. MachineRepo

' ===========================================================
' Notes
' ===========================================================
note top of MachineRepo
  Was: SQL-only repo + separate StateWriter
  for dual-store coordination.
  Now: composes the mirror; every PG status
  write fires an async mirror op alongside.
  Cleaner call graph, one fewer class.
end note

note right of Mirror
  Renamed (heartbeat → redis_mirror) because
  the class owns BOTH:
  - liveness (Redis-authoritative, no PG twin)
  - status mirror (PG twin, now async)
  "Heartbeat" was understating the surface.
end note

note bottom of DeletedWriter
  set_status was the only public method.
  Folds into MachineRepository.update_status.
  Every import of MachineStateWriter is
  retargeted to MachineRepository.
end note

@enduml
